Rule 1 (input must be 4-D NHWC with positive sizes)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 4 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) ≥ 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) ≥ 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 2) ≥ 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 3) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 2 (pooling_ratio list has length at least 4)
{v_2 : list(float)} |= v_2.len ≥ 4
>>
Rule 3 (pooling_ratio length matches 4-D input)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(float)} |= ndim(v_1) = 4 ∧ v_2.len = ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 4 (no pooling on batch and channel dimensions)
{v_2 : list(float)} |= v_2.len ≥ 4 ∧ v_2[0] = 1.0 ∧ v_2[v_2.len - 1] = 1.0
>>
Rule 5 (only height and width ratios may differ from 1.0)
{v_2 : list(float)} |= v_2.len ≥ 4 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : (i = 1 ∨ i = 2) ∨ v_2[i] = 1.0
>>
Rule 6 (height and width pooling ratios must be ≥ 1.0)
{v_2 : list(float)} |= v_2.len ≥ 4 ∧ v_2[1] ≥ 1.0 ∧ v_2[2] ≥ 1.0
>>
Rule 7 (overlapping requires actual spatial pooling)
{v_2 : list(float), v_4 : bool} |= v_2.len ≥ 4 ∧ (v_4 = false ∨ v_2[1] > 1.0 ∨ v_2[2] > 1.0)
>>
Rule 8 (conditional length rule for pooling_ratio)
{v_2 : list(float)} |= if v_2.len > 4 then v_2[0] = 1.0 ∧ v_2[v_2.len - 1] = 1.0 else v_2.len = 4
